= Psi Ward =

{{Plain_Hook
| in_one_sentence    = The Psi Ward is a static area-defense [[Psi Devices|psi device]] that creates a psionic boundary field — a defined spherical, cylindrical, or shaped perimeter inside which all external psionic effects (area psi attacks, [[Psychotronic Generator]], [[Neural Scrambler]]) are excluded by enforcing the null condition Ψ_external(r_boundary) = 0 along the bounding surface.
| everyday_analogy   = A Faraday cage for psionic fields, with the same operating principle: enforce a boundary condition on the relevant field along a closed surface, and the interior becomes electromagnetically (here, psionically) isolated from the exterior. Inside a Faraday cage your phone has no signal, but a transmitter inside the cage can talk to a receiver inside the cage without leaking out. Same logic for the Psi Ward: it's bidirectional — outside attacks can't get in, and inside emissions can't get out (a warded area is psionically invisible). Compared to active defenses ([[Defense Discs]]) that intercept threats one at a time, the Psi Ward is passive infrastructure: once erected, only maintenance power is needed and ALL spectrum, ALL attack types are blocked at the perimeter.
| what_it_predicts   = (1) Boundary condition Ψ_external(r) = 0 for all r on ∂V (the ward surface); (2) Bidirectional — blocks both incoming attacks AND outgoing emissions; (3) All-spectrum effective — covers all psionic frequencies and attack categories; (4) Static, requires only maintenance power once established; (5) Shape-flexible: spherical, cylindrical, or contoured boundaries; (6) Use cases: field hospital dome, command-post cylinder, sensor-outpost sphere, [[Psi Harmonizer]] recovery wards; (7) Real-world parallel: Faraday cage / anechoic chamber / SCIF (Sensitive Compartmented Information Facility).
| if_you_remember_one_thing = The Psi Ward is the area-denial analogue of a Faraday cage — boundary-condition-based passive defense. The framework's claim is engineering, not new physics: if the [[Psi Field]] exists and obeys field-theoretic boundary conditions, then enforcing Ψ = 0 on a closed surface produces a null interior.
}}

{{Way_It_Works
| title  = How a Psi Ward enforces a closed psionic boundary
| step1_label = Establish the geometry
| step1_text  = Decide the shape and extent of the protected volume V (a sphere for field hospitals, a cylinder for command posts, a contoured envelope for a sensor outpost). The boundary ∂V is the surface on which the ward enforces null conditions. Geometry is determined by operational needs: dome over a building, cylinder over a vehicle convoy, custom contour for unusual installations.
| step2_label = Deploy boundary emitters
| step2_text  = Place [[Psi Emitter]] nodes around the boundary, spaced closely enough that their individual exclusion fields overlap. Each emitter generates a local cancellation field tuned to produce destructive interference with any psionic signal crossing its sector of the boundary. Spacing depends on emitter strength and target frequencies.
| step3_label = Synchronise via PsiLink mesh
| step3_text  = All boundary emitters are linked through the [[PsiLink]] mesh and coordinated by [[PsiSys]]. They share a common phase reference so their cancellation fields combine coherently along the entire boundary. Loss of synchronisation creates holes — hence Neural Firewall protection of the mesh itself is critical.
| step4_label = Enforce Ψ_external(r_boundary) = 0
| step4_text  = For any incoming psionic signal Ψ_in(r,t) reaching the boundary, the local emitter produces Ψ_emit(r,t) = −Ψ_in(r,t) at that surface point. Net Ψ = 0 on ∂V. By the linearity of the psi field equation and uniqueness of boundary-value solutions, this forces Ψ = 0 throughout the interior for purely external sources — the warded volume is psionically clean.
| step5_label = Exploit the clean interior
| step5_text  = Inside the ward, the ψ-field is determined entirely by internal sources — making it a controlled environment for sensitive operations: [[Psi Harmonizer]] therapy, [[Psi Scanner]] high-sensitivity sensing, [[Psi Recorder]] reference measurements, [[PsiLink]] secure communication. The bidirectional property is what makes the interior tactically invisible: external sensors can't detect activity within.
| step6_label = Handle limits and failure modes
| step6_text  = Limits: maintenance power must continue; mesh synchronisation must be preserved; boundary emitters are physical hardware and can be physically attacked. Failure mode: loss of one emitter creates a localised hole at that sector. Mitigation: redundant emitter coverage and [[Neural Firewall]] protection of the PsiLink mesh itself. The Psi Ward is robust but not invincible — it's the psionic equivalent of physical fortifications.
}}

